<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <!--
        SETUP NOTE (unset): This overlay deliberately declares NOTHING. It exists to document that the
        `unset` flavor omits both automatic-push flags, which is the third state of
        com.klaviyo.push.automatic_push_token_forwarding:
          - absent  — the SDK forwards tokens delivered to KlaviyoPushService.onNewToken, but does not
                      fetch the token at Klaviyo.initialize() or on foreground (this flavor).
          - "true"  — additionally fetches proactively (see src/automatic/AndroidManifest.xml).
          - "false" — no automatic forwarding at all (see src/manual/AndroidManifest.xml).
        com.klaviyo.push.automatic_push_open_tracking is opt-in, so omitting it means this flavor's
        Activity calls Klaviyo.handlePush() itself.
        Declaring either key with ANY value — including "false" — moves the app out of the absent state,
        so a library merging one of these keys into a host app's manifest would change the host's
        behavior. Do not declare these keys in a library manifest.
    -->

</manifest>
